# restic exclude patterns for kb3lyb-backup.
#
# SYNTAX WARNING: `#` only starts a comment at the BEGINNING of a line. A trailing
# comment becomes part of the pattern, so
#
#     /home/mark/.sdkman        # JDKs, re-downloadable
#
# is one literal path ending in "# JDKs, re-downloadable" and matches nothing at
# all. restic does not warn about patterns that never match, so the exclusion just
# silently does not happen — that is exactly how the first snapshot ended up with
# .sdkman, nvim/mason and the podman overlay store in it. Keep every comment on
# its own line.
#
# Rule of thumb: exclude anything a script can rebuild. Everything here is either a
# cache or reproducible from something already in version control.
#
# NOT excluded on purpose:
#   ~/.var/app   flatpak app DATA lives here (Joplin notes, client configs,
#                Bitwarden state) mixed with caches — only the cache subdirs go.
#   ~/dotfiles   already on GitHub, but tiny, and inline makes a bare-metal
#                restore one step shorter.
#   ~/src        git repos, but local branches and stashes are not pushed.

# --- network mounts (IMPORTANT) ---------------------------------------------------
# ~/OneDrive-InstrumentalID is a fuse.rclone mount of the M365 OneDrive, not local
# storage. kb3lyb-backup already passes --one-file-system, which skips it because
# the mount is a different filesystem; this entry is belt and braces and makes the
# hazard visible rather than implicit in a flag.
#
# Without either guard, restic would walk the mount and DOWNLOAD THE ENTIRE
# ONEDRIVE to copy it onto the NAS: slow, expensive, and pointless since OneDrive
# is already the second copy.
/home/mark/OneDrive-InstrumentalID

# --- caches -----------------------------------------------------------------------
/home/mark/.cache
/home/mark/.npm
/home/mark/.var/app/*/cache
/home/mark/.local/share/Trash

# podman's overlay store. Also the source of the "permission denied" errors on the
# first run: its layer directories are owned by subuid-mapped UIDs inside a user
# namespace, so the plain user cannot read them. All re-pullable.
/home/mark/.local/share/containers

# --- reproducible tooling (rebuilt by kb3lyb-bootstrap) -----------------------------
# pinned by lazy-lock.json, which IS in the dotfiles repo
/home/mark/.local/share/nvim/lazy
# language servers, re-installable via :Mason
/home/mark/.local/share/nvim/mason
# JDKs, re-downloadable with sdk install
/home/mark/.sdkman
# self-updating, re-downloaded by bootstrap
/home/mark/.local/share/JetBrains/Toolbox
/home/mark/.homebrew

# --- game data (large, re-downloadable) ---------------------------------------------
/home/mark/.local/share/Steam
/home/mark/.steam

# --- ephemeral ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.swp
/home/mark/.local/state/nvim/swap
